		{
			description: [
				"A lasting camp needs five things: beds, dependable food, labelled storage, a marked water source, and a waypoint. Build those before filling the base with decorations or machines."
				"Keep spare food, blocks, tools and a shield in an obvious expedition chest. A player returning from a corpse run should not have to search through twenty containers."
				"Light routes as well as rooms. Most early deaths happen between safe places, not inside them."
				"Build the first base around repeatable routines: a safe bed, cooked food, labelled storage, spare tools, and a visible mine entrance. Decoration can begin immediately, but survival infrastructure keeps every later project enjoyable."
			]
