			description: [
				"The server handles ordinary exploration well, but thousands of loose items, animals, hoppers or always-running machines still create work every tick. Prefer controlled farms and storage over giant piles of entities."
				"Switch machines off when they are not producing anything. Avoid permanently loading distant areas unless they perform a useful job, and clean up abandoned boats, minecarts and dropped items."
				"Good engineering is not only fast. It is observable, repairable and quiet when idle."
				"Build the first base around repeatable routines: a safe bed, cooked food, labelled storage, spare tools, and a visible mine entrance. Decoration can begin immediately, but survival infrastructure keeps every later project enjoyable."
